  "summary": "On June 5, 2026 an attacker used social engineering against a third-party contractor of AdaptHealth, a home medical equipment provider, to get the contractor's credentials and access cloud-based business applications, including patient management systems and document storage. The attacker also took a stored password file for insurance billing and external EHR portals. On June 15 the attacker contacted AdaptHealth claiming to have patient files; ShinyHunters listed the company and threatened to leak the data unless paid. Names, contact, demographic, insurance and health information of 4,115,802 people were stolen.",
